WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.640
It is publicly known that you and Hillary
Clinton are friends already for decades.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.350
Friendships in the political world are rare.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.130
What makes it that your friendship has survived?

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:25.900
I have known Hillary for almost 30 years and
I hope that when this conference takes place,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.779
she has been elected president.

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:36.719
We share common values, political values,
but also I think that these are deeply rooted

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:43.460
in our own personal experiences.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:52.519
We have defended these values against
all sorts of people who have used whatever

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.239
means that they could.

00:00:55.239 --> 00:01:10.530
Many of them underhanded, in order to try
and destroy reputations. To attack people personally.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:15.729
To engage in what we have called the politics of personal destruction,

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:20.790
but for political advantage and gain.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:32.240
It is not only a bond of friendship,
but rooted, I think, in our common devotion

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:38.469
to advancing democracy in the country.

00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:43.799
It sounds like a cliché but there it is.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:51.200
We are a year apart in age, we grew up five
miles from each other.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.079
We know very much who we are.

00:01:55.079 --> 00:02:04.500
So, I think that there is a rootedness as
well in our commitment to engagement.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:11.849
Does she realize the enormity of the responsibility
she will get when she is elected president?

00:02:11.849 --> 00:02:24.680
I think if anybody understands the responsibility
of the presidency, it would be Hillary Clinton,

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:35.440
having served in the White House with her
husband and having been Secretary of State

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.629
with another president: Barack Obama.

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:44.890
There are very few people in American history
who have had that sort of background who have

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:49.620
risen to the presidency.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.170
She would be a rare person.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:57.150
Not only as the first woman but simply as
a person to assume that office.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.250
Thank you, Sidney.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.629
I am much looking forward seeing you on the
12th of November in Amsterdam.

